   "text": "I read the structure in sections and assembled one SMILES; the two points I was least sure of are the chain lengths.\n\n- **Left end:** a thalidomide-type unit, 2-(2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl)isoindoline-1,3-dione. Its 4-position carries a tertiary amine nitrogen.\n- **Branches on that nitrogen:**\n  - a CH2C(=O)NH\u2013 arm leading to a six-carbon chain and then a piperazine nitrogen;\n  - a four-carbon chain ending in a secondary NH that is bonded to CH2 on a cyclohexane.\n- **Cyclohexane:** it is 1,4-disubstituted, with the CH2NH carbon on a hashed bond and the indazole nitrogen on a wedge. These are opposite faces, so the ring is trans, and I wrote the stereo accordingly.\n- **Indazole:** a 2H-indazol-2-yl bearing a 6-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl) group and, at position 5, an NH\u2013C(=O) amide to a 6-(trifluoromethyl)pyridin-2-yl ring.\n- **Right-hand side:** the piperazine's other nitrogen is acylated by a para-phenylene carbonyl. That ring carries an NH on a pyrazinone, which has an N-methyl and a C=O. The pyrazinone's aryl group is 2-methyl-3-(4-tert-butylbenzamido)phenyl.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(N2C(=O)c3cccc(N(CCCCNC[C@H]4CC[C@H](CC4)n4cc5cc(NC(=O)c6cccc(C(F)(F)F)n6)c(C(C)(C)O)cc5n4)CC(=O)NCCCCCCN4CCN(CC4)C(=O)c4ccc(Nc5nc(-c6cccc(NC(=O)c7ccc(C(C)(C)C)cc7)c6C)cn(C)c5=O)cc4)c3C2=O)C(=O)N1"
